    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktails\nMargarita\nSherry\nDubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini\nVermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nAperitivo\nApéritif\nDelicia Guadeloupe\nLush snow crab and cold water shrimp in ripe tomato with\ncucumber, corn and pepperoncini.\nFilete de Res a la Mejicana\nGrilled select tenderloin steak with stuffed olives\nin a rich brown sauce.\nPechuga de Ave a la Veracruzana\nTender breast of chicken in a spicy sauce.\nPapa Rellena\nStuffed baked potato\nFrijoles a la Casera\nHome style black beans\nArroz Crillo\nYellow rice Pilaf\nLegumbres Mixtos\nMixed vegetables\nQueso y Galletas\nCheese and biscuits\nCopa Sandunga\nRich vanilla sherbet with ripe mango and bitter sweet chocolate curls.\nCafé\nCafé Descafeinado\nTé",
      "Papa Rellena\nStuffed baked potato\nFrijoles a la Casera\nHome style black beans\nArroz Crillo\nYellow rice Pilaf\nLegumbres Mixtos\nMixed vegetables\nQueso y Galletas\nCheese and biscuits\nCopa Sandunga\nRich vanilla sherbet with ripe mango and bitter sweet chocolate curls.\nCafé\nCoffee\nCafé Descafeinado\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTe\nTea\nCafé Pan Amigo\nCoffee with Kahlúa and whipped cream\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Bénédictine Crème de Menthe\nCognac Napoléon Cointreau Kahlúa\nAmaretto di Saronno\n295.KS",
      "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nIn the mountains north of Peking (Beijing), looking toward Inner Mongolia, is the Great Wall. The largest\nman-made structure on earth, the 3,000 mile wall was begun in the third century B.C. It took over\n200 years to complete. The Peking area also offers such wondrous sights as the Ming Tombs, the\nForbidden City, the Great Hall, Chairman Mao's Memorial and the Temple of Heaven. Shanghai,\nSoochow (Suzhou), Hangchow (Hangzhou), and Canton (Guangzhou), among many other cities,\noffer equally breathtaking vistas.\nA visit to the People's Republic of China is a unique and totally remarkable experience: now, only\n14 hours away on Pan Am's 747SP Clippers.\nSPAN AM.\n2001.080.265"
    ],
